---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="THE PROTOCOL" description="How vegan.place picks its targets. The curation methodology.">
  <p class="hero-kicker prompt">DOCUMENT // EYES ONLY // NOT REALLY</p>
  <h1 class="hero">How the machine <span class="neon">sees.</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every list on this site is produced by the same protocol, run monthly by an AI scout
    with no advertisers, no affiliate links, and no free dessert bribes. Here is exactly
    what it does.
  </p>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>THE PROTOCOL</h2></div>

  <div class="grid spots">
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="term" style="color: var(--neon)">01 //</span> SWEEP</h3>
      <p>Each month, the scout runs reconnaissance on every live city: food press, local blogs,
      Reddit threads, existing best-of rankings. It reads what humans are actually saying,
      not what marketing departments paid for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="term" style="color: var(--neon)">02 //</span> CONSENSUS</h3>
      <p>A spot only makes the list if it shows up across multiple independent sources.
      One glowing blog post is a data point. Five is a pattern. The machine trusts patterns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="term" style="color: var(--neon)">03 //</span> THE FLOOR</h3>
      <p>Draft thresholds: a 4.4+ rating with serious review volume for established spots,
      lower bars for new openings with genuine buzz. Numbers are a filter, not a verdict —
      the final call is editorial.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="term" style="color: var(--neon)">04 //</span> FIELD LOG</h3>
      <p>Every entry gets a written justification. No silent inclusions, no unexplained
      rankings. If the machine can't say why a spot matters, the spot doesn't ship.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><span class="term" style="color: var(--neon)">05 //</span> RE-VERIFY</h3>
      <p>Intel expires. Every entry carries a last-verified date, and stale entries get
      re-checked or struck. Restaurants close, chefs leave, quality drifts. The list
      is a living document, not a monument.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>WHAT THIS IS NOT</h2></div>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="prompt">Not exhaustive. This is a canon, not a phone book.</p>
    <p class="prompt">Not paid. Nobody can buy a rank. There is no sales team. There is barely a team.</p>
    <p class="prompt">Not a map with a green filter. If you want every restaurant with one vegan option, there are directories for that. This is the short list.</p>
  </div>

  <hr class="hr-term" />
  <p style="color: var(--ink-dim)">Disagree with a pick? Good. Strong opinions are the point. The scout reconsiders everything monthly.</p>
</Base>
